---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About — PixelForge"
	description="PixelForge is a single-purpose, free browser-based image converter. Learn why it exists, how it works, and why your files never leave your device."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
		<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">About PixelForge</h1>

		<div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[#4A4234]">
			<p>
				PixelForge does one thing: it converts image files from one format
				to another, entirely inside your browser. There's no account to
				create, no upload to wait on, and no server that ever sees your
				files.
			</p>
			<p>
				We built it as a single-purpose tool on purpose. Rather than bundling
				a dozen unrelated utilities behind one confusing homepage, PixelForge
				is exactly, only, an image converter &mdash; so it loads fast, stays
				focused, and does the one job well.
			</p>
			<h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#221B10]">
				How it works
			</h2>
			<p>
				When you choose or drop a file, your browser decodes the image
				locally and draws it onto a hidden canvas element &mdash; the same
				machinery your browser already uses to display images on any
				webpage. That canvas is then re-encoded into whichever format you
				picked (PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF, or BMP) and handed back to you as a
				normal downloadable file. Two formats your browser can't read
				natively &mdash; HEIC/HEIF (the format iPhones save photos in) and
				TIFF &mdash; are decoded on-device with small, purpose-built
				libraries before the same canvas pipeline takes over.
			</p>
			<p>
				Because everything happens on your device, nothing you convert is
				ever transmitted, logged, or stored anywhere. Close the tab and it's
				gone, exactly as if you'd never opened it.
			</p>
			<h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#221B10]">
				Why it's free
			</h2>
			<p>
				PixelForge is supported by small, unobtrusive advertising rather than
				subscriptions or paywalls. There's nothing to sign up for and no
				limit on how many images you convert.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
